From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:20:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10773/11362] [outer-loop] Widen induce-failure note clips so
 the pool-truncation diagnostic survives (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6860)

The 2026-09-02 live r11l run stored three 179-char notes: the 29-char
'split induce: engine failed: ' prefix plus a 150-char clip, cut mid-word
at 'budg'. The dropped tail carried the n_ctx pool size and the
'RAISE -c / CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_N_CTX' fix instruction. Four independent
local clips (150 split-induce, 160 resample error, 240 refinement-round
message, 300 proposer_note) meant widening any one still lost the tail
at the next site.

One shared constant now bounds all five sites:
INDUCE_FAILURE_NOTE_CLIP = 500 in arc_executable_world_model.py, wide
enough for the longest generate() message (server failures cap at 400)
plus the longest wrapper prefix. Rejected alternative: a separate
structured diagnostic field -- more surface for the same information,
and every existing consumer (rerun_exp6221 startswith-match, the
liveness witness substring checks) already reads the message string.

Consumer check: rerun_exp6221_infra_crashed_cells.py prefix-matches
(unaffected); test_proposer_note_is_truncated_to_300 pinned the local
300 literal and is rewritten against the shared constant.

Mutation-proven: reverting the engine-site clip to [:150] turns 2 of 3
new tests RED; source restored byte-identical (cmp) and re-verified
green. Step 6 check: test_no_storage_site_narrows_the_clip_below_the_
constant pins each site to the shared constant so a local literal
cannot creep back.

